# Chaos: creature spawn fade-in and hit recoil (O232; client/BASE.md "0151"; src/client/chaosrecoil.h (new, pure), creature.h/.cpp;
# after 0001-0150).
# Two small creature animations, both pure draw-time maths from one start time per creature (nothing else is kept).
#  * Spawn fade-in: Creature::onAppear, in the branch of a creature that is new or comes back into view (m_removed), stores
#    the start time when chaos::recoil::wantsFade allows it: the option is on and it is not the local player. Creature::
#    draw then calls DrawQueue::setOpacity (the call the floor fading and the death fade of 0139 use) over the items of the
#    outfit, with alpha 0 -> 1 over 180 ms (smoothstep). No setScale, setRotation or clip, so the draw cache is not flushed.
#    The name, the bars and the light are not faded. The option is the existing `deathFade` (Creature.setDeathFade).
#  * Hit recoil: Creature::setHealthPercent calls startRecoil(old, new) next to startHitTint of 0142, same trigger (health
#    went down, creature on the map and already shown, new health above 0), same option (`hitFlash`, Creature.setHitTint). The
#    drawn position is moved 1 px (2 px for a hit of 10% or more, times the sprite size over 32) away from the local player,
#    the usual attacker, or in a small random direction when the player is the creature itself, on its tile or on another
#    floor. The offset eases back to 0 in 120 ms ((1 - u)^2). Creature::draw adds it to `dest` only (the parameter is now
#    drawDest and `dest` a local copy), map draw only, so the name and the bars stay still. A creature cannot restart its
#    recoil inside 100 ms.
#  * No new option, no new text, no Lua change: the panel keeps its height and there is no new pt-BR key.
# Cost when idle: two int compares per drawn creature. Active: one opacity pass over that creature's items for 180 ms, or
# an add of two ints for 120 ms.
# Known: the attacker is taken as the local player, so a hit by a summon or a party member pushes the same way; a hit that
# does not change the 1% step is not seen; the click box and the shadow of the creature move with the nudge; a layered
# outfit (colour templates) fades through the atlas, which uses the queue colour, and when the atlas is full that item is
# drawn without the fade (as in 0139); a shader item ignores opacity. At login, or on a floor change, every creature in view
# is new and fades in.
# Checked: applies after 0001-0150 on the base tree; creature.cpp shows the same 3 base errors under g++ -fsyntax-only; the
# header passes its test.
# Not built, linked or run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
